# Editor-side configuration for clangd.
#
# clangd's IncludeCleaner has two halves, and this project takes them
# differently on purpose:
#
#   UnusedIncludes  Strict  -- "you include <span> but never use it". A handful
#                              of real, actionable findings. Kept on.
#
#   MissingIncludes None    -- "you use std::size_t, so include <cstddef>
#                              directly even though <array> already provides
#                              it". That direction produced ~280 findings when
#                              it was tried through clang-tidy's
#                              misc-include-cleaner, nearly all noise, which is
#                              why that check is disabled in .clang-tidy too.
#                              Off here so the two tools agree.
#
# An include that only exists for one platform's #ifdef branch will still be
# reported as unused on the others; mark those `// IWYU pragma: keep`, as
# paths.cpp does for <string>.
Diagnostics:
  UnusedIncludes: Strict
  MissingIncludes: None
